{
  "name": "VIP email alert to Telegram",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "pollTimes": {
          "item": [
            {
              "mode": "everyMinute"
            }
          ]
        },
        "simple": false,
        "filters": {
          "q": "in:inbox -from:me",
          "readStatus": "unread"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "62985dba-a612-5f52-9a8f-66956fb1e2d5",
      "name": "New email",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmailTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "raw",
        "jsonOutput": "{\n  \"config\": {\n    \"telegram_chat_id\": \"123456789\",\n    \"vip_senders\": [\n      \"boss@example.com\",\n      \"@bigclient.com\"\n    ]\n  }\n}",
        "includeOtherFields": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "f45da664-c0f7-56d8-895e-8460d6914133",
      "name": "Settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        240,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const cfg = $('Settings').first().json.config;\nconst vips = (cfg.vip_senders || []).map((v) => String(v).toLowerCase().trim()).filter(Boolean);\nreturn $('New email').all().filter((i) => {\n  const from = String((i.json.from && i.json.from.value && i.json.from.value[0] && i.json.from.value[0].address) || '').toLowerCase();\n  return vips.some((v) => v.startsWith('@') ? from.endsWith(v) : from === v);\n}).map((i) => ({ json: {\n  from: (i.json.from && i.json.from.text) || '', subject: i.json.subject || '(no subject)',\n  snippet: String(i.json.text || i.json.snippet || '').replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').slice(0, 300) } }));"
      },
      "id": "b00d5320-768f-5002-8ba4-9abab9f59815",
      "name": "Is it from a VIP?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        480,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "chatId": "={{ $('Settings').first().json.config.telegram_chat_id }}",
        "text": "=VIP email from {{ $json.from }}\n{{ $json.subject }}\n\n{{ $json.snippet }}",
        "additionalFields": {
          "appendAttribution": false
        }
      },
      "id": "390257a8-15d7-5428-b5ef-d8ee587d7871",
      "name": "Telegram me",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegram",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        720,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## VIP email alert to Telegram\nWhen an email arrives from someone on your VIP list (or a whole company domain), you get a Telegram message with the subject and first lines.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "dbcbe582-ad29-5899-b649-b358e24b74ea",
      "name": "Note: what this does",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Setup (about 10 minutes)\n1. Create a Telegram bot with **@BotFather** and add its token as a Telegram credential in n8n. Send your bot a message, then get your chat ID (for example from @userinfobot).\n2. Open **Settings**: your Telegram chat ID and the VIP list (full addresses, or `@domain.com` for a whole company).\n3. Connect Gmail and Telegram.\n4. Run it once with test data, then switch to **Active**.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "8d13ab43-40fa-55ab-9e83-b7272b73d9e7",
      "name": "Note: setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        400,
        -420
      ]
    }
  ],
